<title>INDIA: India forex reserves ease to $23.43 bln on Feb 14.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves ease to $23.43 bln on Feb 14.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves fell to $23.43 billion on February 14, 1997 from $23.99 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Feb 14	Feb 7	  Feb 16</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,320	19,868	 15,988</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,097	 4,097	  4,587</p>
<p>    SDRs				    11	    28	     49</p>
<p>    Total			     23,428	23,993	 20,624</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
